{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For it was little that you had before me, etc. and YHWH blessed you by my foot.</b> He says: from the day my foot came to your house, blessing came to you. And so Laban acknowledged: נחשתי ויברכני ה' בגללך. And the blessing was that the flock burst beyond the boundary of the natural order; at first he entrusted into his hand only seventy, and they rose to sixty myriad, and some say to one hundred and twenty myriad. And so they expounded in Bereshit Rabbah: מעט אשר היה לך לפני — R. Shimon in the name of R. Hezekiah said: מעט — seventy. It says מעט here and it says elsewhere (Deuteronomy 26:5) ויגר שם במתי מעט — just as there it is seventy, so too here seventy, etc." "<b>When shall I provide for my own house also.</b> That I shall endeavor for the benefit of my house, just as you have endeavored until now in the labor that I have labored for you. Or he explained: 'When shall I do for my house' — as I have done for your house. <b>And as for what it says,</b> ארעה צאנך אשמור — the meaning is: I will be a hired guardian."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:33.997491053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}